{"id": "EUVD-2026-59667", "enisaUuid": "aa761b69-90b8-308e-bb2e-9c97a21db535", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: use pskb_network_may_pull() for transmit path header pulls\n\nIn vxlan_xmit(), arp_reduce(), and vxlan_mdb_entry_skb_get(), pskb_may_pull() was\nbeing called to verify the availability of network layer headers (ARP, IPv6/ND,\nIP/IPv6 MDB keys).\n\nHowever, during transmit skb->data points to the MAC header, so skb_network_offset(skb)\nis ETH_HLEN (14 bytes). Using pskb_may_pull(skb, len) only checks len bytes from skb->data\nrather than skb_network_offset(skb) + len, which can leave part of the network header\nin non-linear frags.\n\nReplace these remaining pskb_may_pull() calls with pskb_network_may_pull() to properly\naccount for the MAC header offset.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:48", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/371425d4be7795e9158388af9eee0201e6047410", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb01c51950c3ff3c76acdd54b85ab38ccc2a8bb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6146901881f09ef063eb34ad389f63231f8486f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94dee751aad627b3645d424b5d0c736d394573e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7076a34b6e33315dc160b4612bfea1c597495585", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9553558b48db54ac9273e6b98d7263ef5c1a329"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74474", "GHSA-59jj-4qq4-v9f9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07dffca7-687f-32cf-b392-ea2801a92fb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "14c3192a-3dd3-3b9f-8733-25f26b8eeaca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "3444b61c-25c7-3a2c-a6db-e83657216239", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, 